          "filename": "Chun Quoit - geograph.org.uk - 1065611.jpg",
          "caption": "Chun Quoit Chun Quoit is a chambered tomb consisting of four upright stones about a metre and a half in height, three of which support a fairly circular 2-3 metre wide capstone.  The name of the Quoit is derived from the Cornish \"Chy-an-Woone\" which means \"the house on the downs\".",
