          "filename": "Chûn Quoit - geograph.org.uk - 1477165.jpg",
          "caption": "Chûn Quoit Quoit is the Cornish name for a type of megalithic chambered tomb. They consist of a number of large stones set upright to support a massive horizontal capstone, thus forming a small chamber which was used to house the remains of the dead. The whole structure would then be covered in earth to form a large burial mound.",
